          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+homotopy+theory"} topological homotopy theory
            %em fundamental theorem of covering spaces
            says that for a sufficiently well-behaved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            which sends a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"}> permutation representation
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p#PathLifting
            This is a basic instance of the general principle of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/PathLiftingInCoveringSpace-230214.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %p
            It follows in particular that for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            coincides with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X,x)
            itself (for any basepoint
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the first place.
          %p
            This is closely related to the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                      %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                      %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd_{/\esh X} \simeq \infty Grpd^{\esh X}
            restricts to an equivalence between the subcategories of bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to \esh X
            with 0-truncated fibers and of set-valued functors on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Pi_1(X)} \simeq Set^{\esh X}
          %p
            (Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh X
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape
            of the topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+via+cohesive+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} hence
            its
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoid"}
                fundamental
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h2#statement Statement
          #FundamentalTheoremOfCoveringSpaces.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (fundamental theorem of covering spaces)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+path-connected+topological+space"} locally path-connected
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-locally+simply-connected+topological+space"} semi-locally simply-connected topological space
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  extracting the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Fib
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib_{E}
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reconstructing+a+covering+space+from+monodromy"} reconstructing a covering space from monodromy
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Rec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \; Rec(\rho)
            %p
              constitute an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cov
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Fib
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi Rec
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cov(X)
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{Fib}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{Rec}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\simeq}
                    Set^{\Pi_1(X)}
            %p
              between the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+covering+spaces"} category of covering spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+representations"} groupoid representations
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              With the standard definitions of the two functors, both are in fact inverse
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              of categories instead of just
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences+of+categories"} equivalences of categories
              (meaning that the required
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
              from the composites of the two functors to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
              are componentwise
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalities"} equalities
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in Set^{\Pi_1(X)}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of permutation representations.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta_{\rho}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\rho \longrightarrow Fib(Rec(\rho))
            %p
              First consider what the right hand side is like: By
              %a{:href => "reconstruction+of+covering+spaces+from+monodromy#ElementaryReconstructionCoveringSpace"} this def.
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rec
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rec
              and
              %a{:href => "monodromy#CoveringSpaceMonodromy"} this def.
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib
              we have for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              an actual equality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fib(Rec(\rho))(x) = \rho(x)
                    \\,.
            %p
              To similarly understand the value of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib(Rec(\rho))
              on morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma] \in \Pi_1(X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \colon [0,1] \to X
              be a representing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path"} path
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "covering+space#CoveringSpacePathLifting"} this lemma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of paths
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\gamma_i\}_{i \in \{1,n\}}
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  regarded as morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma_i]
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
                  they
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} compose
                  to
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\gamma]
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [\gamma] = [\gamma_n] \circ \cdots \circ [\gamma_2] \circ [\gamma_1]
              %li
                %p
                  each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_i
                  factors through an open subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \subset X
                  over which
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Rec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rec(\rho)
                  trivializes.
            %p
              Hence by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functoriality
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib(Rec(\rho))
              it is sufficient to understand its value on these paths
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fib(Rec(\rho))([\gamma_i]) = \rho([\gamma_i])
                    \\,.
            %p This means that if we take
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo =
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta_\rho(x) \colon \rho(x) \overset{=}{\longrightarrow} Fib(Rec(\rho))
            %p
              to be the above identification, then this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              and hence in a particular a natural isomorphism, as required.
            %p
              It remains to see that these morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_\rho
              are themselves natural in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \rho \to \rho'
              the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ρ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi eta
                                    %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi ρ
                                      %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Rec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi Fib
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Rec
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Rec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\rho &amp;\overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \rho'
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{eta_\rho}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\eta_{\rho'}}}
                    \\\
                    Fib(Rec(\rho))
                    \&amp;\underset{Fib(Rec(\phi))}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Fib(Rec(\rho'))
                    }
            %p
              commutes as a diagram in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rep
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(\Pi_1(X), Set)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              the corresponding component diagram commutes. But by the above this is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo =
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Rec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi Fib
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Rec
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Rec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\rho(x) &amp;\overset{\phi(x)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \rho'(x)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{=}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{=}}
                    \\\
                    Fib(Rec(\rho))(x)
                    \&amp;\underset{Fib(Rec(\phi))(x) }{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Fib(Rec(\rho'))(x)
