            %p and hence this means that the top and bottom horizontal morphism are in fact equal. Direct unwinding of the definitions shows that this is indeed the case.
            %p
              Conversely, given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cov
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in Cov(X)
              a covering space, we need to exhibit a natural isomorphism of covering spaces of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon_E
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Rec(Fib(E)) \longrightarrow E
                    \\,.
            %p
              Again by
              %a{:href => "reconstruction+of+covering+spaces+from+monodromy#ElementaryReconstructionCoveringSpace"} this def.
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rec
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rec
              and
              %a{:href => "monodromy#CoveringSpaceMonodromy"} this def.
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib
              the underlying set of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rec(Fib(E))
              is actually equal to that of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
              on underlying sets is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %p
              By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+path-connected+topological+space"} locally path-connected
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-locally+simply+connected+topological+space"} semi-locally simply connected
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subset X
              an open path-connected subset and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              a point with the property that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(U,x) \to \pi_1(X,x)
              lands is constant on the trivial element, that the open subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \{\hat x\} \subset p^{-1}(U)
              form a basis for the topology of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Fib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rec(Fib(E))
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rec
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rec
            %p
              It remains to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_E
              is itself natural in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_E
              are in fact equalities, this follows by direct unwinding of the definitions.
            %p
              This establishes an equivalence as required. In fact this is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
          %h2#applications Applications
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+the+circle+is+the+integers"} fundamental group of the circle is the integers
          %h2#in_homotopy_type_theory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncation+modality"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                \-truncation
          %p
            Indeed, in HoTT a covering space over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is usually defined as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Sets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \colon X \to \mathsf{Sets}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x \colon X} C(x)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} proj
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{proj}_1 \colon \sum_{x \colon X} C(x) \to X
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{Sets}
            is a
            = succeed "-type," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  \\Vert X \Vert_1 \to \mathsf{Sets}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\big(
                  X \to \mathsf{Sets}
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since the 1-truncation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert X \Vert_1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            %br/
          %p#InCohesiveHomotopyTypeTheory
            Or rather, more faithful to the traditional concepts in topology, it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            which turns a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+type"} geometric homotopy type
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoid"}
              fundamental
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh X
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+via+cohesive+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} shape via cohesive path ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vert \esh X \Vert_1
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
            says that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo ♭
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  \\esh X \to \mathsf{Sets}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\big(
                  X \to \flat \mathsf{Sets}
                  \\big)
                  \\,,
          %p or, equivalently, that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo ♭
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                    %mi Sets
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  \\Vert \esh X \Vert_1 \to \mathsf{Sets}
                  \\big)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\big(
                  X \to \flat \mathsf{Sets}
                  \\big)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi Sets
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat Sets
            is the actual classifier for covering spaces in the generality of cohesive (e.g. topological) homotopy types. This reflects the fundamental theorem of covering spaces as traditionally understood in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
          %p
            This is the topic of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} dcct, sec. 3.8.6
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1310.7930v1.pdf#page=358"} p. 358
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CherubiniRijke20"} Cherubini &amp; Rijke 2020, Thm. 8.7
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"}> fundamental group
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+cover"} universal cover
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "smooth+homotopy#HomotopyOfSmoothPathsRelativeToTheirEndpoints"} homotopy of smooth paths relative to their endpoints
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck%27s+Galois+theory"} Grothendieck's Galois theory
          %h2#references References
          %p On the classical theory:
          %p A detailed treatment is available in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topologie Algébrique
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-49361-8"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-49361-8
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#tomDieck2008
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
              , Thm. 3.3.2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic topology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ems-ph.org/books/book.php?proj_nr=86"} doi:10.4171/048
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/diecktop.pdf"} pdf
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Waldhausen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedhelm+Waldhausen"}> Friedhelm Waldhausen
                , around p. 122 of
                %em Topologie
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-bielefeld.de/~fw/ein.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Moller11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesper+M%C3%B8ller"}> Jesper Møller
                , Thm. 7.8 in:
                %em The fundamental group and covering spaces
                (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1106.5650"}> arXiv:1106.5650
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ku.dk/~moller/f03/algtop/notes/covering.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Moller-FundamentalGroup.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+theory"} cohesive homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} dcct, sec. 3.8.6
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1310.7930v1.pdf#page=358"} p. 358
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#CherubiniRijke20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Cherubini"}> Felix Cherubini
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
              = succeed "," do
                %em Modal Descent
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.09713"} arXiv:2003.09713
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129520000201"} doi:10.1017/S0960129520000201
